= Localhost dashboard
On the repo you'll find a folder: `dashboard`.
This folder contains a python script that emulate a SCADA dashboard.
You will use this dashboard all along the lab, the first step is to run it locally on your laptop and analyse the traffic with wireshark.
You must analyse the http traffic generated by this dashboard. 

#task[Run and analyse dashboard locally][
  Write a small report with basic information as capture / display filter you used and what you found on packet.
  You can illustrate with wireshark screenshots and concise explanation. The dashboard generates http traffic on port #traffic-port-http. In this task, we are focus on the content of the payload. 

  #subtask[
    On PyCharm, open the `main.py` file in the `dashboard` folder and run it. 
  ]

  #subtask[
    Open Wireshark and select the loopback / localhost interface. Choose the right capture filter.
  ]

  #subtask[
    Select specific display filter to get only the `http` traffic and show in your report a packet in depth from the header to the json payload
  ]

]

#pagebreak()

= IIoT Rack and LAN
Since this task, we will use the IIoT (Industrial Internet of Things) Rack.
This rack (@fig:iiot-rack:hardware) contains several devices will see later. We are now focusing on the Edge Router on top right.
You will connect your laptop to this router, experiment DHCP and analyse local traffic. To connect on the router you can use the user: #iiot-rack-router-user with the password: #iiot-rack-router-pwd

#figure(
  image("../res/img/iiot-rack-hardware.svg", width: 60%),
  caption: [IIoT Rack - hardware]
) <fig:iiot-rack:hardware>

#task[LAN connection][
  You previously ran the dashboard locally and connect to it with the same computer.
  You will now exchange with a partner.
  One student will be the server and another the client.
  You must observe the difference with the previous task and write it down on your report. 

  #subtask[
    Connect both your laptop on the edge router. You will receive an IPv4 by DHCP.
  ]

  #subtask[
    Find your ip address on this LAN. Explain on your report which method you use. \
    // Tips: One method is to use `ipconfig` for Windows, `ip config` on MacOS / Linux.
  ]

  #subtask[
    One student start the python script, the other connects to the webpage with the right IP address.
    Analyse the traffic with Wireshark on both computer. You need to modify the interface on Wireshark.
    Show and explain the main difference with the previous task in your report. 
    
    #warningbox[
      Maybe you will have some issues to communicate with another laptop, specially on Windows. If you experience any issues, don't hesitate to ask for help. It can be caused by an aggressive antivirus.
    ]

  ]

]
#bonus[Lease time][
  Find your lease time. Show and explain and your report how you find this info. Explain what is the lease and the consequence to have a shorter / longer lease. 
]

